  "verbalization": "Lupulone is shown to interact with the CD276 antigen through a multi-step mechanism involving the NQO1 protein. The evidence suggests that Lupulone targets NQO1, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including (3Ar,4As,8R,8Ar,10As)-8-Hydroxy-1-Isopropylidene-3A,8A-Dimethyl-5-Methylene-Dodecahydro-Benzo[F]Azulen-2-One and Laur-11-En-10-Ol. These compounds all ultimately direct their activity to the CD276 antigen. The final scores indicate a consistent and plausible pathway, suggesting that Lupulone may exert its effects through a similar mechanism, potentially by inhibiting NQO1 or modulating its downstream targets. The integration of multiple evidence paths supports a biologically plausible link between Lupulone and CD276, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and their shared interaction with CD276 suggests a potential role in immune regulation or cellular stress response, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this.",
